  <running_head>I. IACOMOTI</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Tentauit, eheu! sub duce Barbaro</l>
    <l n="2">Gallus? Tyrannorumque signa</l>
    <l n="3">Hospita Guisiadum sequutus</l>
    <l n="4">Funesta Gallis praelia cinibus</l>
    <l n="5">Impune mouit? Ruraque feruido</l>
    <l n="6">Sulcata Francorum labore</l>
    <l n="7">Marte suo populata vidit?</l>
    <l n="8">Quum sceptra Genti Gallica perfida,</l>
    <l n="9">Et fraudulento prodidit hospiti:</l>
    <l n="10">Quum iussa vellet subiugatos</l>
    <l n="11">Francigenas Lotharinga ferre?</l>
    <l n="12">Tali superbis milite, Guisie,</l>
    <l n="13">Regnumque poscis, quidlibet impotens</l>
    <l n="14">Sperare, per vastas ruentis</l>
    <l n="15">Dum patriae furit ille cades.</l>
    <l n="16">Sic regna Stirpi debita regiae</l>
    <l n="17">Galloque captas aduena principi?</l>
    <l n="18">Sic prisca Legum sacra turbas</l>
    <l n="19">Et Salicae pia iura Normae?</l>
    <l n="20">Te blandienti somnus imagine,</l>
    <l n="21">Te mentis error ludit amabilis:</l>
    <l n="22">Quum sceptra Gallorum lacertis</l>
    <l n="23">Grandia non paribus prehensas.</l>
    <l n="24">Qui regna terris diuidit omnibus,</l>
    <l n="25">Qui regna firmat legibus additis</l>
    <l n="26">Tremendus author, Gentibusque</l>
    <l n="27">Iura dedit, violanda nulli:</l>
    <l n="28">Qui cuncta rubri fulminis ignibus</l>
    <l n="29">Terret</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Verse text; the words "Terret" at lower right may be a catchword. Long s rendered as s; the "Stirpi", "Galloque" lines and the words "Guisiadum", "Guisie" are as printed. Some words in the right margin are faint show-through and are omitted.</notes>
